msgid ""
"<p>This field should contain your name, or the name of the person who created the photograph. If it is not appropriate to add the name of the photographer (for example, if the identify of the photographer needs to be protected) the name of a company or organization can also be used. Once saved, this field should not be changed by anyone. This field does not support the use of commas or semi-colons as separators. \n"
"This field is limited to 32 ASCII characters.</p>"
msgstr "<p>Hier schall Dien Naam oder de vun den Fotograaf stahn. Is dat nich mööglich oder nich wullt (wenn a.B. den Fotograaf sien Naam schuult warrn mutt), kannst Du hier ok den Naam vun en Sellschap oder Organisatschoon bruken. Na't Sekern mutt nüms dat mehr ännern. Dat Feld ünnerstütt keen Kommas oder Streekpünkt as Trennteken un kann tohööchst 32 ASCII-Tekens bargen</p>"

#. +> trunk
#: utilities/setup/setupidentity.cpp:96
msgid "Author Title:"
msgstr "Maker sien Titel:"

#. +> trunk
#: utilities/setup/setupidentity.cpp:101
msgid ""
"<p>This field should contain the job title of the photographer. Examples might include titles such as: Staff Photographer, Freelance Photographer, or Independent Commercial Photographer. Since this is a qualifier for the Author field, the Author field must also be filled out. \n"
"This field is limited to 32 ASCII characters.</p>"
msgstr ""
"<p>Hier schall den Fotograaf sien Profeschoon-Beteken stahn. Bispillen sünd \"Produktenfotograaf\", \"Freeschapen Fotograaf\" oder \"Fotokünstler\". Dit is en Angaav bito dat Maker-Feld, dor muttst Du ok wat infögen.\n"
"Dat Feld kann tohööchst 32 ASCII-Tekens bargen.</p>"

#. +> trunk
#: utilities/setup/setupidentity.cpp:115
msgid "Credit and Copyright"
msgstr "Dank un Copyright"

#. +> trunk
#: utilities/setup/setupidentity.cpp:118
msgid "Credit:"
msgstr "Dank:"

#. +> trunk
#: utilities/setup/setupidentity.cpp:123
msgid ""
"<p>(synonymous to Provider): Use the Provider field to identify who is providing the photograph. This does not necessarily have to be the author. If a photographer is working for a news agency such as Reuters or the Associated Press, these organizations could be listed here as they are \"providing\" the image for use by others. If the image is a stock photograph, then the group (agency) involved in supplying the image should be listed here. \n"
"This field is limited to 32 ASCII characters.</p>"
msgstr ""
"<p>(liek as Anbeder): Mit dat Anbeder-Feld kannst Du angeven, wokeen dat Bild praatstellt. Dat mutt nich jümmers de Maker wesen, wenn he för en Narichtenagentur arbeidt, as Reuters oder Associated Press. Disse Bedrieven köönt denn hier stahn, se stellt dat Bild för den Bruuk praat. Kummt dat Bild ut den Vörraat vun en Agentur, schall se hier stahn.\n"
"Dit Feld kann tohööchst 32 ASCII-Tekens bargen.</p>"

#. +> trunk
#: utilities/setup/setupidentity.cpp:130
msgid "Source:"
msgstr "Born:"

#. +> trunk
#: utilities/setup/setupidentity.cpp:135
msgid ""
"<p>The Source field should be used to identify the original owner or copyright holder of the photograph. The value of this field should never be changed after the information is entered following the image's creation. While not yet enforced by the custom panels, you should consider this to be a \"write-once\" field. The source could be an individual, an agency, or a member of an agency. To aid in later searches, it is suggested to separate any slashes \"/\" with a blank space. Use the form \"photographer / agency\" rather than \"photographer/agency.\" Source may also be different from Creator and from the names listed in the Copyright Notice.\n"
"This field is limited to 32 ASCII characters.</p>"
msgstr ""
"<p>Dat Feld \"Born\" warrt för den Orginaaleegner oder den Eegner vun't Copyright bruukt. Na't Opstellen vun't Bild schull nüms dat mehr Feld ännern. Dat warrt noch nich verdwungen, man liekers, bruuk dat Feld bitte as bloots eenmaal schriefbor. As Born schall en Persoon, en Agentur oder en Agenturliddmaat angeven warrn. As Ünnerstütten för later Söökanfragen giff bitte vör un achter Dwarsstreek Freetekens in, also nich \"Fotograaf/Agentur\", man beter \"Fotograaf / Agentur\". De Born kann wat anners wesen as de Maker oder de Naams bi Copyright.\n"
"Dit Feld kann tohööchst 32 ASCII-Tekens bargen.</p>"

#. +> trunk
#: utilities/setup/setupidentity.cpp:144
msgid "Copyright:"
msgstr "Copyright:"

#. +> trunk
#: utilities/setup/setupidentity.cpp:149
msgid ""
"<p>The Copyright Notice should contain any necessary copyright notice for claiming the intellectual property, and should identify the current owner(s) of the copyright for the photograph. Usually, this would be the photographer, but if the image was done by an employee or as work-for-hire, then the agency or company should be listed. Use the form appropriate to your country. USA: &copy; {date of first publication} name of copyright owner, as in \"&copy;2005 John Doe.\" Note, the word \"copyright\" or the abbreviation \"copr\" may be used in place of the &copy; symbol. In some foreign countries only the copyright symbol is recognized and the abbreviation does not work. Furthermore the copyright symbol must be a full circle with a \"c\" inside; using something like (c) where the parentheses form a partial circle is not sufficient. For additional protection worldwide, use of the phrase, \"all rights reserved\" following the notice above is encouraged. \n"
"In Europe you would use: Copyright {Year} {Copyright owner}, all rights reserved. \n"
"In Japan, for maximum protection, the following three items should appear in the copyright field of the IPTC Core: (a) the word, Copyright; (b) year of the first publication; and (c) name of the author. You may also wish to include the phrase \"all rights reserved.\"\n"
"This field is limited to 128 ASCII characters.</p>"
msgstr ""
"<p>De Kopeerrecht-Angaav schall all nödige Informatschonen bargen, de dat Recht an't intellektuelle Egendom kloorstellt un angeven, wokeen dat opstunns hett. Normalerwies is dat de Fotograaf, man wenn dat en Opdragarbeidt weer oder he för en Bedrief arbeidt, schall de hier stahn. Bruuk de Form, de för Dien Land gellt. USA: &copy; {Johr vun't eerste Apenmaken} Naam vun den Rechtenholler, a.B.: \"&copy; 2005 Klaas Achterndiek\". Ansteed dat \"&copy;\"-Symbool laat sik ok dat Woort \"Copyright\" oder de Afkörten \"copr\" bruken. In en Reeg Länner gellt aver bloots dat Symbool wat. Ok de Formen \"(c)\" un \"(C)\" langt nich. Goot is ok, wenn Du achter de baven angeven Bemarken de Wöör \"all rights reserved\" bruukst.\n"
"In Europa is en propper Form: \"Copyright {Johr} {Rechtenholler}, all rights reserved\".\n"
"In Japan schöölt disse Indrääg binnen dat Copyright-Feld stahn: a) dat Woort \"Copyright\", b) dat Johr vun't eerste Apenmaken, un c) de Naam vun den Maker. Ok hier kannst Du \"all rights reserved\" tofögen.\"\n"
"Dit Feld kann tohööchst 128 ASCII-Tekens bargen.</p>"

#. +> trunk
#: utilities/setup/setupidentity.cpp:175
#, fuzzy
msgid "<b>Note: These information are used to set <b><a href='http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Extensible_Metadata_Platform'>XMP</a></b> and <b><a href='http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IPTC'>IPTC</a></b> tag contents. There is no limitation with XMP, but note that IPTC text tags only support the printable <b><a href='http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ascii'>ASCII</a></b> character set, and tag sizes are limited. Use contextual help for details.</b>"
msgstr "<p><b>Beacht bitte</b>: Disse Informatschonen warrt na <b><a href='http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Extensible_Metadata_Platform'>XMP</a></b>- un <b><a href='http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/IPTC-NAA-Standard'>IPTC</a></b>-Feller sekert. För XMP gifft dat keen Grenz, man för IPTC laat sik bloots de druckboren <b><a href='http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ascii'>ASCII</a></b>-Tekens un en fastleggt Bookstaventall bruken. Bruuk dat Rechtsklickmenü, wenn Du mehr weten wullt.</p>"

