#. +> trunk
#: utilities/setup/setupmetadata.cpp:204
msgid "<b><a href='http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exif'>EXIF</a></b> - a standard used by most digital cameras today to store technical information (like aperture and shutter speed) about an image."
msgstr "<b><a href='http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Exif'>EXIF</a></b> is en Standard, den de mehrsten modernen Kameras bruukt, wenn se technische Informatschonen över't Bild (so as Brennwied un Belichtentiet) sekert."

#. +> trunk
#: utilities/setup/setupmetadata.cpp:208
msgid ""
"<br>"
"<b><a href='http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IPTC'>IPTC</a></b> - an older standard used in digital photography to store photographer information in images."
msgstr ""
"<br>"
"<b><a href='http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/IPTC-NAA-Standard'>IPTC</a></b> is en öller Standard för de Digitaalfotografie, mit den sik Informatschonen na Biller inbetten laat."

#. +> trunk
#: utilities/setup/setupmetadata.cpp:213
msgid ""
"<br>"
"<b><a href='http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Extensible_Metadata_Platform'>XMP</a></b> - a new standard used in digital photography, designed to replace IPTC."
msgstr "<p><b><a href='http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Extensible_Metadata_Platform'>XMP</a></b> is en nieg Standard in de Digitaalfotografie. He schall maal IPTC utwesseln.</p>"

#. +> trunk
#: utilities/setup/setupmime.cpp:98
msgid ""
"<p>digiKam attempts to support all of the image formats that digital cameras produce, while being able to handle a few other important video and audio formats.</p>"
" "
"<p>You can add to the already-appreciable list of formats that digiKam handles by adding the extension of the type you want to add. Multiple extensions need to be separated by a space.</p>"
msgstr ""
"<p>DigiKam versöcht, dat all Bildformaten ünnerstütt warrt, de de Digitaalkameras bruken doot, un dor blang noch en Reeg anner wichtig Video- und Klangdatei-Formaten.</p>"
" "
"<p>Du kannst de List mit Dateiformaten, mit de digiKam wat anfangen kann un de al recht groot is, wat tofögen, wenn Du de Verwiedern för den Dateityp angiffst. Mehr as een Verweidern laat sik mit Freetekens dor twüschen ingeven.</p>"

#. +> trunk
#: utilities/setup/setupmime.cpp:113
msgid "Additional &image file extensions (<a href='image'>Currently-supported types</a>):"
msgstr "Bilddatei-Verwiedern bito (<a href='image'>Opstunns ünnerstütt Typen</a>):"

#. +> trunk
#: utilities/setup/setupmime.cpp:117
msgid ""
"<p>Here you can add the extensions of image files (including RAW files) to be displayed in the Album view. Just put \"xyz abc\" to display files with the xyz and abc extensions in your Album view.</p>"
"<p>You can also remove file formats that are shown by default by putting a minus sign in front of the extension: e.g. \"-gif\" would remove all GIF files from your Album view and any trace of them in your database. They would not be deleted, just not shown in digiKam.</p>"
"<p><b>Warning:</b> Removing files from the database means losing all of their tags and ratings.</p>"
msgstr ""
"<p>Hier kannst Du de Albenansicht mehr Bilddatei-Verwiedern (ok Rohdateien) tofögen. Giff eenfach \"xyz abc\" in, wenn Du Dateien mit de Ennen *.xyz un *.abc bruken wullt.</p>"
"<p>Ok standardwies ünnerstütt Dateien laat sik mit en vöransett Minus-Teken ut de List wegdoon: \"-gif\" deit a.B. all GIF-Dateien ut de Datenbank weg, man nich vun de Fastplaat.</p>"
"<p><b>Wohrschoen:</b> Wenn Dateien ut de Datenbank wegdaan warrt, kaamt ok all ehr Slötelwöör un Beweerten weg!</p>"

#. +> trunk
#: utilities/setup/setupmime.cpp:131 utilities/setup/setupmime.cpp:169
#: utilities/setup/setupmime.cpp:207
msgid "Revert to default settings"
msgstr "Op Vörinstellen torüchsetten"

#. +> trunk
#: utilities/setup/setupmime.cpp:149
msgid "Additional &movie file extensions (<a href='video'>Currently-supported types</a>):"
msgstr "&Filmdatei-Verwiedern bito (<a href='video'>Opstunns ünnerstütt Typen</a>):"

#. +> trunk
#: utilities/setup/setupmime.cpp:153
msgid ""
"<p>Here you can add extra extensions of video files to be displayed in your Album view. Just write \"xyz abc\" to support files with the *.xyz and *.abc extensions. Clicking on these files will play them in an embedded KDE movie player.</p>"
"<p>You can also remove file formats that are supported by default by putting a minus sign in front of the extension: e.g. \"-avi\" would remove all AVI files from your Album view and any trace of them in your database. They would not be deleted, just not shown in digiKam.</p>"
"<p><b>Warning:</b> Removing files from the database means losing all of their tags and ratings.</p>"
msgstr ""
"<p>Hier kannst Du de Albenansicht mehr Videodatei-Verwiedern tofögen. Giff eenfach \"xyz abc\" in, wenn Du Dateien mit de Ennen *.xyz un *.abc bruken wullt. Wenn Du disse Dateien anklickst, speelt en inbett KDE-Videoafspeler ehr af.</p>"
"<p>Ok standardwies ünnerstütt Dateiformaten laat sik mit en vöransett Minus-Teken ut de List wegdoon: \"-avi\" deit a.B. all AVI-Dateien ut de Datenbank weg, man nich vun de Fastplaat.</p>"
"<p><b>Wohrschoen:</b> Wenn Dateien ut de Datenbank wegdaan warrt, kaamt ok all ehr Slötelwöör un Beweerten weg!</p>"

#. +> trunk
#: utilities/setup/setupmime.cpp:187
msgid "Additional &audio file extensions (<a href='audio'>Currently-supported types</a>):"
msgstr "&Klangdatei-Verwiedern bito (<a href='audio'>Opstunns ünnerstütt Typen</a>):"

#. +> trunk
#: utilities/setup/setupmime.cpp:191
msgid ""
"<p>Here you can add extra extensions of audio files to be displayed in your Album view. Just write \"mp7\" to support files with the *.mp7 extension. Clicking on these files will play them in an embedded KDE audio player.</p>"
"<p>You can also remove file formats that are supported by default by putting a minus sign in front of the extension: e.g. \"-ogg\" would remove all OGG files from your Album view and any trace of them in your database. They would not be deleted, just not shown in digiKam.</p>"
"<p><b>Warning:</b> Removing files from the database means losing all of their tags and ratings.</p>"
msgstr ""
"<p>Hier kannst Du de Albenansicht mehr Klangdatei-Verwiedern tofögen. Giff eenfach \"mp7\" in, wenn Du Dateien mit de Ennen *.mp7 bruken wullt. En Klick op disse Dateien speelt se denn mit en inbett KDE-Klangafspeler af.</p>"
"<p>Ok standardwies ünnerstütt Dateien laat sik mit en vöransett Minus-Teken ut de List wegdoon: \"-ogg\" deit a.B. all OGG-Dateien ut de Datenbank weg, man nich vun de Fastplaat.</p>"
"<p><b>Wohrschoen:</b> Wenn Dateien ut de Datenbank wegdaan warrt, kaamt ok all ehr Slötelwöör un Beweerten weg!</p>"

#. +> trunk
#: utilities/setup/setupmime.cpp:275
#, kde-format
msgid ""
"<p>You have chosen to remove the following image formats from the list of supported formats: <b>%1</b>.</p>"
"<p>These are very common formats. If you have images in your collection with these formats, they will be removed from the database and you will lose all information about them, including rating and tags.</p>"
"<p>Are you sure you want to apply your changes and lose the support for these formats?</p>"
msgstr ""
"<p>Du wullt de nakamen Bildformaten ut de List vun ünnerstütt Formaten wegdoon: <b>%1</b>.</p>"
"<p>Disse Formaten sünd bannig begäng. Wenn Dien Sammeln Biller mit disse Formaten bargt, warrt se tosamen mit all ehr Informatschonen ut de Datenbank wegdaan. Ok ehr Beweerten un Slötelwöör kaamt weg.</p>"
"<p> Wullt Du Dien Ännern för ünnerstütt Dateiformaten redig bruken?</p>"

#. +> trunk
#: utilities/setup/setupmime.cpp:321
#, kde-format
msgid ""
"<p>Files with these extensions will be recognized as images and included into the database:<br/>"
" <code>%1</code></p>"
msgstr ""
"<p>Dateien mit disse Verwiedern warrt as Biller kennt un na de Datenbank opnahmen:<br/>"
" <code>%1</code></p>"

#. +> trunk
#: utilities/setup/setupmime.cpp:331
#, kde-format
msgid ""
"<p>Files with these extensions will be recognized as movie files and included into the database:<br/>"
" <code>%1</code></p>"
msgstr ""
"<p>Dateien mit disse Verwiedern warrt as Videodateien kennt un na de Datenbank opnahmen:<br/>"
" <code>%1</code></p>"

#. +> trunk
#: utilities/setup/setupmime.cpp:341
#, kde-format
